<<~ aka "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/RFC-2119#/normative-language">>

<<^ code="&#x0002;">>

<<~ ahu #/head>>

! The Empty Subject

The Empty Subject names a check that RAN, measured NOTHING, and reported SUCCESS.

It wears no defect of its own. The logic holds, the assertion stands correct, the run exits clean — and the set it walked carried no members, or the field it read wore a spelling nothing writes, or the condition it refuses cannot arise. A gate in this state produces ''the cleanest output it has ever produced'', which reads to every hand downstream as the strongest possible evidence that the ground it guards stands sound.

''The failure inverts the ordinary one.'' A wrong check goes red and a hand comes running. This one goes green and recruits the reader to its own silence — and the greener it reads, the longer it stands. Measured TEN times in a single day, each instance wearing a different coat.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/ooda-ha>>

✶ detect any gate, witness, weld or `--check` that WALKS a set, SCANS for a spelling, or refuses a condition.
⏿ orient by the one question below — never by reading the assertion, which reads correct in every instance.
◇ decide which of the three cure shapes the instrument takes; the house sanctions three and wants no fourth.
▶ act — plant the violation and require the reading to MOVE, then put the defect back and watch the cure NAME it.
↺ a cure claimed and never planted stands as the same failure one layer up: an instrument certified by an instrument nobody collided.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/the-question>>

!! The one question

> ''If its subject vanished tomorrow, would this go RED — or report clean?''

The question asks about the SUBJECT, never about the logic. A hand who reads the assertion instead will find it correct every time, because in this failure the assertion IS correct — correct about an empty set.

Three answers sort every instrument:

* ''ARMED'' — it carries a floor on its subject's size, or an explicit vector asserting the code under test RAN, or a revert-verify.
* ''VACUOUS-CAPABLE'' — it could pass over an empty, absent or unreachable subject. The reading MUST name exactly WHAT would have to vanish; a hand who cannot name it has not measured the instrument.
* ''DEAD'' — it measures nothing TODAY. Proving this takes one act: run the matcher against the real corpus and show it returning zero.

''The verdict comes off a measurement, never off a reading.'' Every DEAD instance in the record read plausible to a careful eye and returned zero to a shell.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/cures>>

!! The three cure shapes

The house sanctions three and wants no fourth. They compose; the strongest cures take two.

# ''A FLOOR ON THE SUBJECT'S SIZE.'' Any gate that WALKS a set MUST assert the SET'S SIZE before it asserts anything about the set's members, and the size MUST print beside the verdict — a clean line that never states its subject's size lets a reader mistake a walk over seven hundred carriers for a walk over none. An absent subject reads RED, never clean: `nothing to compare` and `nothing wrong` name different facts, and an instrument that collapses them reports cleanest exactly where it saw least.
# ''A SUBSTITUTION / MUTATION WALK.'' Take the REAL corpus, inject the violation, and require the reading to MOVE. A fixture pins the grammar; only the corpus pins the reader.
# ''A CONTROL THAT READS FALSE, plus a REVERT-VERIFY.'' Put the defect back and watch the cured instrument NAME it. A cure shown only passing repeats the failure it cures.

''PROVING A CURE BITES IS PART OF THE CURE.'' A repaired instrument MUST be shown to REFUSE, and the refusal quoted verbatim where the next hand reads it — the commit message, or this carrier. A cure that has only been shown passing has been shown nothing.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/law>>

!! The law

The node MUST ask ''if its subject vanished, would this go red'' BEFORE building any gate, witness or weld — the question belongs at design time, where it costs one line, rather than at census time, where it costs a day.

A gate that WALKS a set MUST assert the set's size before asserting anything about its members, and MUST print that size beside its verdict.

A gate whose SUBJECT is absent MUST exit non-zero. It MUST NOT exit clean with a note.

A probe that reads a SPELLING (a field key, a decorator, a call form, a control code binding) MUST fail when it reads that spelling on NOBODY. A field no reader can find never disagrees with anything.

A cure MUST ship its planted red, quoted. The node MUST NOT claim a cure it has only watched pass.

''A permanently-red witness and a permanently-green one fail the same way'' — each teaches a reader to stop reading it. The house answers a standing red with a declared, printed, counted debt against a ceiling that only shrinks; it answers a standing green with the floor above.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/diagnostic>>

!! The tells, each measured

Every coat below was worn by a live instrument in this tree.

* ''A retired spelling.'' The probe binds a form the corpus stopped writing — a colon where a call binds with `=`, a decorator with empty parentheses where one now carries an argument. Greppable: run the literal against the corpus and read the count. Zero names it.
* ''An absent subject read as a clean one.'' A missing file, a moved surface, an unbuilt shore — reported as //nothing to compare// and exited 0.
* ''A window narrower than the carrier.'' A byte prefix, a `slice(0, N)`, a flat read where the tree nests. The instrument goes blind in the direction that reports clean.
* ''A scan that cannot reach where its subject must appear.'' A self-clearing weld scanning one package while the caller it waits for can only land in another certifies an absence it never looked for.
* ''A floor beneath the ground.'' A count-floor set below what the corpus already holds, so half the subject could vanish under it.
* ''A check over an empty span.'' A hash over nothing matches its own recomputation.
* ''A condition that cannot arise.'' A one-row ledger produces no crossing, so the vector proving the gate REFUSES passes by having nothing to refuse.
* ''A comment claiming the floor the code omits.'' The header states the law and nothing beneath it counts — worse than a plain omission, because a hand auditing the instrument is told the guard stands.
* ''A weld counting the declaring file's own export as a caller.''
* ''A `test.todo`, or a skipped vector nobody re-reads.''

''The diagnostic'': if the instrument reports green, ask what number it printed. An instrument that names no count has not told you whether it looked.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/worked>>

!! Worked examples, by commit

Each cure below planted its red, quoted it, and reverted it.

* `e103acd1d` — the `carrier-shape` family floors, cured by a SUBSTITUTION WALK. The floors stood over a corpus where the second code of each family appears exactly ONCE and no carrier's marks turn on it, so a reader could drop half of every family and stay green.
* `185dae028` — `offering-antigen.test.ts`, a self-clearing weld whose caller scan read one `src/` while its first honest caller could only land in another package. Green forever, certifying an absence it never looked for.
* `tools/hearths-gate-witness.sh` — the ★ RED vector drove off the ledger's first two `trailer =` lines; at one standing hearth no path can cross, so the vector proving the gate REFUSES would have passed by having nothing to refuse. Cured by ARMING against a fixture built from the ledger's OWN rows, live and closed, while every pass-through CONTROL keeps reading the real ledger — and the run PRINTS which ledger each half read.
* `522ee4479` — `tools/frame-parity.mjs`, DEAD. Its corpus probe asked `code:"&#x00NN;"` where the corpus writes `code="&#x00NN;"` 2848 times and the colon form zero times, so all seven marks routed to //stands on paper alone// and BOTH pattern seams were skipped on every run. Cured by admitting both bindings and flooring on the count PROBED. The revert-verify: a pattern deliberately aimed at a mark nothing writes, under the uncured tool, exits 0 printing //every mark ... patterns against a real carrier//.
* `530c76ce7` — `tools/surface-parity-witness.sh`, three holes in a file already keeping the cure on its own other side. Its uncured reading states the family in the instrument's own words: //MCP tools: 0   CLI doors reachable: 0// followed by //every MCP tool answers to a CLI door//, exit 0.
* `156ee3bfe` — `tools/typecheck-witness.sh`, whose comment read //A run that checked nothing must not read as a run that found nothing// with nothing beneath it counting.
* `ee4ec9434` — `tools/meme-coordinates-witness.sh`, printing a verdict with no number and reading only the first 4000 bytes, blind to three carriers that declare their coordinate past that mark.
* `4855ae145` — `tools/domain-registry-witness.sh`, where three of four checks walk one regex's output and all three pass over an empty list.

<<~/ahu>>

